      "justification": "Customers with a prior successful campaign outcome subscribe at 76.3% under treatment (261/342) vs 61.6% under control (210/341), a +14.7pp lift (two-proportion z ~ 4.16, p ~ 3e-5). This survives Bonferroni correction across the ~7-10 segment-level tests I ran (adjusted p ~ 3e-4), and would survive a much larger hypothetical search. The effect replicates within contact channel: cellular +14.7pp (194/318 vs 240/317, z ~ 3.98, p ~ 7e-5) and telephone +14.4pp (16/23 vs 21/25, same direction, underpowered at n=48). Arms are balanced (341 vs 342). Other poutcome segments show no treatment effect: failure -0.6pp and nonexistent -0.15pp. Non-success contact splits are also null (cellular -0.65pp, p ~ 0.27; telephone +0.54pp, p ~ 0.28). SignalGuard's VERIFIED_SIGNAL on the contact query reflected the contact main effect rather than a treatment effect, so I did not report it. The weak overall lift (+0.3pp raw) is consistent with a concentrated responder segment (~3.3% of customers) diluted by a large null majority. This was a post-hoc exploratory finding, so a confirmatory holdout test is advisable before wide rollout."
